    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCharming Former Presbytery in a Peaceful West Limerick Setting\n \nNestled in Kimehere, Shanagolden, Co. Limerick, this attractive former presbytery offers a rare opportunity to acquire a property full of character, history, and potential in a beautiful rural setting. Surrounded by the peaceful countryside of West Limerick, the property enjoys a quiet and private location while still being within easy reach of local villages, amenities, and transport links.\n \nThis distinctive home combines the appeal of an older period property with the opportunity for a purchaser to create a truly special residence. The house is ideally suited to those seeking a family home, country retreat, or restoration project with plenty of charm and original character. The subject property has the benefit of full planning permission (Planning Ref: 25300) for change of use of existing derelict presbytery (which is a Protected Structure) and out buildings to one new detached dwelling house and permission for elevational alterations and installation of a new domestic wastewater treatment system, new boundaries and all associated site works.\n \nThe internal accommodation once completed will comprise of: open plan kitchen/dining/living room, utility room, tv room, 2 ground floor bedrooms and a bathroom, two first floor bedrooms and a shower room.\n \nLocated just a short distance from Shanagolden village, the property benefits from access to everyday amenities including shops, schools, church, sports facilities, and local services. The surrounding area is well regarded for its strong community spirit, scenic countryside, and convenient access to nearby towns such as Foynes, Newcastle West, and Limerick City. The area also offers easy access to a range of recreational amenities including walking routes, sporting clubs, and the Shannon Estuary.\n \nThis is a unique opportunity to purchase a property of character in a sought-after rural location, offering peace, space, and enormous potential for further enhancement.\n \nFeatures:\nStone Wall\nRanch Railing Fence\nClose proximity to the port of Foynes\nCommuting distance to Limerick City\nWater and electricity connections available at roadside subject to relevant connection fees\nEligible for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant subject to an individual purchasers suitability"
      },
      {
